# Shared Component Rules

Every component must:

Support Light Mode

Support Dark Mode

Support Mobile

Support Keyboard Navigation

Support Accessibility

Use Shared Theme Tokens

Be Fully Typed

Be Reusable

Remain Stateless whenever possible

Expose only necessary props

Avoid duplicated functionality

---

# Component Composition Rules

Small components compose larger ones.

Example

CareerHero

uses

Button

Badge

ProgressRing

StatisticCard

BookmarkButton

ShareButton

Divider

Never duplicate child components.

---

# Naming Convention

Component names use PascalCase.

Examples

CareerHero

SkillCard

ProjectCard

MentorCard

ProgressRing

CourseCard

RoadmapTimeline

---

# Folder Organization

components/

layout/

navigation/

career/

roadmap/

learning/

projects/

portfolio/

certificates/

progress/

mentor/

assessment/

dashboard/

community/

forms/

feedback/

shared/

ui/

---

# Development Rules

Never create a new component if an existing one can be extended.

Prefer composition over inheritance.

Prefer configuration over duplication.

Keep components focused on a single responsibility.

Business logic belongs outside the component.

Every reusable UI element added to AI Career OS must first be documented in this specification before being implemented.